 "admissions_overview": {
  "summary": "In Botswana you apply directly to each institution, usually soon after BGCSE results come out. Admission is based on points from six BGCSE subjects: the University of Botswana, for example, asks for at least six subjects with no grade below E, English Language among them, and a minimum of 34 points for degree programmes (30 for diplomas), with higher points for competitive programmes. Government sponsorship for citizens is handled by the Department of Tertiary Education Financing (DTEF), which uses its own points system.",
  "official_url": "https://www.ub.bw",
  "notes": "University of Botswana programme names are from its official list of undergraduate programmes; for the other institutions the entries name the fields of study listed in the World Higher Education Database, not exact programme titles. Requirements change every year, so check each institution before applying."
